TYPE ERROR: Foreign declaration 'rename' redeclares a built-in runtime name with a NARROWER effect row: the built-in performs <FileWrite dst, FileWrite src>, this declaration claims <FileWrite src>, which does not cover <FileWrite dst, FileWrite src>. A local extern whose name matches a stdlib/runtime.mdk built-in is always lowered as that built-in, whatever the local signature says — so 'rename' really does perform <FileWrite dst, FileWrite src>, and every caller typechecked against this declaration would be told it does not. Declare the built-in's own row `<FileWrite dst, FileWrite src>` (a WIDER row such as `<IO>` is also accepted — over-declaring is safe), or rename the extern to a name the runtime does not already define
TYPE ERROR: Foreign declaration 'writeFile' redeclares a built-in runtime name with a NARROWER effect row: the built-in performs <FileWrite path>, this declaration claims <FileWrite content>, which does not cover <FileWrite path>. A local extern whose name matches a stdlib/runtime.mdk built-in is always lowered as that built-in, whatever the local signature says — so 'writeFile' really does perform <FileWrite path>, and every caller typechecked against this declaration would be told it does not. Declare the built-in's own row `<FileWrite path>` (a WIDER row such as `<IO>` is also accepted — over-declaring is safe), or rename the extern to a name the runtime does not already define
